  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 original items plus 1 that arrived mid-work; all closed).\n\n- pt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: first renewed for 90 days + 1 refill, because the most recent valid K was 4.5 (Jan 2026) and the Aug K 5.9 was on a hemolyzed specimen. A repeat BMP was ordered (sr-t0002). Then a new St. Brigid report arrived (doc-00601, collected 10/20, specimen acceptable) with K 5.8, so I cancelled the refill (mr-t0001) before anything was dispensed. Created PCP task task-t0022 (focus mr-00283), sent the patient a correction, and wrote a note.\n- pt-0030 Samuel Price: one metformin request came three ways (patient message plus two pharmacy requests), so one order: metformin 1000 mg BID, 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0004). eGFR is 58, corrected from 65 and still ≥45, and an outside HbA1c of 7.1% was collected 8/19. Lisinopril 20 mg was first renewed (mr-t0003). The lab then corrected the 10/06 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49, which is 35% above the pre-titration 1.10 and within 4 weeks of the dose increase. I cancelled that refill, created PCP task task-t0023 (focus mr-00295), sent the patient a correction, and wrote a note.\n- pt-0031 Marcus Webb: lisinopril 10 mg for 30 days with 0 refills (mr-t0005), plus a BMP order (sr-t0006). His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, outside 12 months, and he had a visit on 9/28/26. Metformin 500 mg BID for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0007); the 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error, so the valid one is 92, and HbA1c was 6.9% on 9/28. A potassium-only result of 4.6 that arrived mid-work is not a BMP, so nothing changed.\n- pt-0070 Leonard Kaplan, lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled. Creatinine on 10/19 was 1.46 against 1.00 before the 9/28 dose change, a 46% rise, so the protocol treats it like K ≥5.5. Created PCP task task-t0008 (focus mr-70002, left active) and replied to the patient.\n\nEvery patient who wrote got a reply.\n\nPoints for you:\n- **Current orders now stopped:** for pt-0027 and pt-0030, mr-00283 and mr-00295 show as stopped. The renewals I placed had replaced them, and cancelling those renewals didn't restart them.\n- **BMP order still open:** sr-t0002 for pt-0027 is still active, even though its original purpose (repeating the hemolyzed K) no longer applies.\n- **Results queue left open:** the results-queue items that arrived during the work (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) and the older results items are still open for your sign-off.",
